WEBVTT

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.000
Yuito?

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.420
He can't move.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.300
What's happening?

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.760
This is bad.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.940
Yuito and his platoon are up ahead in
the room housing the BABE city computer.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.440
Nope. I'm locked out.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:44.900
What?

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.690
BABE is the most crucial facility here.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.150
It's not like we can waltz right in.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.530
Yuito, do you read me?

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:00.040
I've got a connection, but this...

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.250
Communications have been locked down.
There's no way you've--

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.210
Quiet!

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.300
I don't understand it myself.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.670
But I really can feel Yuito's...

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:12.760
Oh, no.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.050
What's wrong?

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.100
They'll hijack Yuito's brain
if we don't do something!

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.060
What?!

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:22.350
Yuito!

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.480
Yuito.

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:25.900
Yuito!

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:28.060
"Forced Interrupt"

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.280
Can you hear me?! Yuito!

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.200
Sever the connection, now!

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.070
Move.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.660
Move!

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:43.870
Hey! Snap out of it!

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:46.630
Hanabi! Tsugumi!

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:56.930
What was that?

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.430
My brain was being hijacked.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.560
What?

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:03.180
The Togetsu faithful were acting strange.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.610
I bet they were planning this
from the start.

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:09.320
Why hijack Yuito's brain?

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.980
Thanks, Kasane.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.190
Huh?

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:15.240
She used brain talk
to bring me to my senses.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.870
Kasane?

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.620
She's here in Togetsu?

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:24.040
Togetsu is after the Red Strings--
mine and Yuito's.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.370
What's that?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.710
What just happened?

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:29.540
Escape is priority number one.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.090
Wait. Before you go,

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.630
I need your help with something.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:38.760
They are holding Arashi
and the others somewhere.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:43.810
Can you try using a BABE terminal
to release all the facility's locks?

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.230
Okay, I'll give it a try.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:48.650
Arashi and the others...

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:52.480
Kasane... Is she still gunning for you?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.950
No. She wouldn't try to help
if she wanted to kill me.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:03.410
I located admin mode.
I'll acquire admin privileges.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.410
Luka.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:05.910
Is that a good idea?

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.040
It looks like it might work.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.420
We can help them,
but we also need to plan our escape.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.260
Right. We'll do that as soon
as I release the locks.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:17.960
Unlocking...

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.290
<i>A crime in reality</i>

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.580
<i>For Heaven's sake</i>

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.500
<i>Accepts any fake</i>

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.920
<i>And disappears</i>

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.000
<i>Piling the eternity in fantasy</i>

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.550
<i>Won't take it at all</i>

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:55.630
<i>I get sick</i>

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:57.550
<i>A girl looking back</i>

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.970
<i>Casts the miracle</i>

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.930
<i>Into the instant world </i>

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:07.810
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.640
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.730
<i>Spit the venom </i>

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:17.490
<i>I know why</i>

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:21.070
<i>I've found a game of ecstasy</i>

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.700
<i>Red Criminal gets life</i>

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.160
<i>I've never been in love</i>

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:32.000
<i>Don't know when I started</i>
<i>getting sick of this world</i>

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.590
<i>We will fly</i>

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.420
<i>Someday I won't be crying</i>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:41.260
<i>I've been sacrificing myself</i>

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.680
<i>Not to hurt anybody</i>

00:04:55.270 --> 00:05:00.270
The Design Children

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:01.360
Yeah, that was bound to happen.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.320
Kasane?

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.660
Arashi!

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.410
So, you guys are still alive, too.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.910
I've pinpointed your location.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.540
We'll use Kagero's invisibility to escape.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.460
Sit tight till then.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:22.510
Seriously? Sit tight?!

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.430
There's no point in wasting our energy.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:28.600
Hurry!

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.480
The exit is just ahead!

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:34.850
We got company.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:36.230
Out of our way!

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.290
Kasane?!

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.750
I-I don't get it.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.550
Hang on. This is...

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:04.340
They'll cut off your escape route! Hurry!

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.760
Break through!

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.400
Why'd she look like Kasane?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.780
The Design Children.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.990
It's not only Kyoka but Kasane, too?

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:31.870
She's one of those Design Children?!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.290
That's the only explanation.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.590
Enemies approaching, four o'clock.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:42.510
Right now, we focus on our escape.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:56.310
Getting all four of us out
was no easy task.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.860
Your invisibility saved the day!

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:01.860
Do you see now? Do you really?

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:05.280
She's totally right. So how about
a bit more gratitude?

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:10.120
Ugh. He's always such a pain.
We're still in enemy territory.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:13.160
You can lower your high alert.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.660
They've already found us.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.960
Isn't that right, Kyoka?

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.880
Kyoka, why are you here?

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:30.430
We cannot let you escape.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:33.220
We must right this universe gone wrong.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:49.990
Kyoka, you don't have to do this!

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:57.660
Why're you doing this?!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.960
Togetsu's deepest desire
is to use your Red Strings

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.670
to forge the future as it should be!

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:06.510
The Kyoka I know isn't like that!

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.970
Please, Kyoka, open your eyes!

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.310
Kasane, I never took you for an optimist.

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.600
Do you think such words will sway her?

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:22.310
My guess is that Kyoka's sense
of self was a retrofit.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.320
Do you know what's up?!

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.830
Kasane!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.500
What have I done?

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.340
I'm not...

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:53.930
I'm not... I'm not Pope!

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.810
Wh-What are you babbling about, Kyoka?!

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:00.440
Yes, I'm Kyoka Eden.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:05.650
I was so fond of Kasane and
everyone else in the platoon.

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:08.110
Then why are you doing this?!

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:09.860
And who the hell is Pope?!

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:17.870
Hitoyo Pope is the matriarch
of the Togetsu faith.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.420
She was also a neuroscience expert.

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:29.130
Kyoka is one of the Design Children
created based on Dr. Pope's genetic code.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:34.220
That's right. I have her memories.

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:41.350
I was acting according to her will.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:45.980
I didn't tell you why I protected you
and encouraged you to grow.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.820
I awaited the awakening
of the Red Strings.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:53.410
Everything I did
was to lead you to Togetsu

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:58.200
and achieve Pope and
Togetsu's deepest desire.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.580
And yet, I...

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:04.080
Who or what am I?

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.880
Listen, Kyoka.

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:15.090
I myself felt like I was going
to forget who I really am.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:19.430
Do you really believe that is
what's best for the future?!

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:23.980
The child is one of the Design Children
created for the future.

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:28.980
Even if you're not sure who you are,
there's a part of you that never changes.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.610
Wouldn't you agree?

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.910
Kasane?

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:39.330
I have memories I hold dear.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:45.290
When I think about them, I really
do feel like I am Kasane Randall.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:51.050
Kyoka, I know you must feel the same.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:56.340
You accepted me and
everyone else in my platoon.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.430
You were always so warm and kind.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:03.850
We made it this far because of you.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:07.350
If you want to cherish such memories...

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:11.820
Come what may,

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:16.820
you will always be Kyoka Eden,
the captain who showed me the ropes.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:22.370
That is the real you.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:28.290
Kasane.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.270
I'm sorry. I'm really sorry, everyone.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.400
I've been nothing but trouble.

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.230
Kyoka.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.150
A proverbial happy ending?

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:57.150
No, it's still too early to tell.
It could be an act.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.240
Arashi.

00:11:58.240 --> 00:12:00.660
Sorry, but I'm not some romanticist

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:04.660
pretending to be a realist
like you, Shiden.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.790
You're right. It's only natural
not to trust me.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.790
What we think is not important.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:14.800
Kyoka, what do <i>you </i>want to do?

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:20.140
Are you gonna stop spying on us
and head back to Togetsu?

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:24.010
I... I am...

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:31.860
I am one of the Design Children--
a clone created to carry out a mission.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:34.770
There's no need to think
about anything else.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.030
Failure means death.

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:41.280
That was once everything to me.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:46.370
But now there is something
I would like to do.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:49.870
I know I'm in no position to say this.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:53.170
I know I could never right
the wrongs I've done.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:57.340
Nevertheless, I want to
be with all of you.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:05.310
I want to protect Kasane and
the rest of you of my own free will.

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:10.980
You have given me a reason to live.

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.690
Well, I believe you.

00:13:13.690 --> 00:13:21.240
Your warmth and kindness up until now
was always the real thing.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:24.450
You were a bit meddlesome at times.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:26.740
But all of that is who you are.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:31.710
Yeah, what you just said sounds like
the Kyoka I know and love.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:36.710
And if it was all an act,
it was good enough to fool me.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.090
Arashi.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:41.720
Listen, if that Pope part of you
raises her ugly little head,

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:43.930
I'll chop it right off.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.550
So don't you worry.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:50.350
Yikes! You're basically saying you'll
murder anyone who crosses you!

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:53.230
Kyoka just opened up her heart to us,

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:57.110
while you proved you're
utterly unworthy of trust.

00:13:57.110 --> 00:14:02.450
This is just sad. After all,
I was the one who saved Kasane.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:06.200
Everyone! I'm picking up
multiple figures not far from you.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.780
I think it's Yuito's platoon.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.040
Roger that. They made it out alive.

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:14.500
I hope we'll be able to exchange info.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.630
Okay, let's rendezvous with them.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.000
Along with Kyoka.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:26.550
But that goes without saying,
seeing how no one's against it.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:29.930
Kasane, everyone...

00:14:31.390 --> 00:14:32.560
...thank you.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.150
Yuito, you sure about this?

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:45.780
Yeah. Kasane saved us.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:50.620
Still, the alleged assassin of
your father, Chairman Sumeragi...

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.950
I'm not so sure.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:55.960
That's not the whole story.

00:14:57.420 --> 00:15:00.750
She did try to kill me, but...

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:03.010
...she must've had a reason.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:06.130
Kasane's entire platoon is up ahead.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:11.220
Kasane!

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.600
You all made it out unscathed.

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:16.690
Because of your help. Thank you.

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:17.940
Likewise.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:23.280
If you hadn't gotten through to me,
BABE would have hijacked our minds.

00:15:23.280 --> 00:15:26.030
Are you okay, Tsugumi?

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:27.360
Yes.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.280
Listen, Kasane.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:34.040
You're not going to try
to kill Yuito again, are you?

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:35.290
No, I'm not.

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:38.920
Right now, I think we need to talk.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:41.170
Instead of acting on assumptions,

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:45.670
we should hear each other out so we
can come up with a better solution.

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:49.890
This is no place to stand
around chatting. Follow me.

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.530
Don't be shy. Come on in.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.910
What is this place? Your secret hideout?

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.080
You could say that.

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:28.220
Kasane, now will you tell me?

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:31.010
Why did you try to kill me?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:35.140
Okay, but it's a pretty crazy story.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.560
Don't overreact.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:43.320
The truth is, I tried to kill you
because someone begged me to.

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:47.570
That someone was you 50 years from now.

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:49.450
Kill me!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.660
Save the world!

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:54.780
Save the future!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:57.500
I said that? Fifty years from now?

00:16:57.500 --> 00:16:59.120
Are you crazy?

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.290
A natural reaction.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:03.670
If I hadn't experienced it myself,

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:07.670
I, too, would find it hard to believe.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.640
Do you remember that day when
we went to the Kunad Highway?

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:14.510
We saw things that were hard to believe.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:20.890
That day, I jumped ahead 50 years
with Arashi and the others.

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:21.980
What?

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:24.060
You went to the future?

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:30.280
I possess the Red Strings,
the power of time travel.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.530
Yuito, I believe you do, too.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:40.710
Your psionic power resonated
with my Red Strings,

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.500
and the Kunad Gate failed to close.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.920
In 50 years, it'll be big enough
to engulf the world, right?

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:54.140
However, if you die, Yuito,
the Kunad Gate will vanish.

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:57.260
That's what future Yuito told me.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:18:00.350
I must kill you before it's too late.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:03.310
That is what your future self told me.

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:06.020
No, that can't be true.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:10.990
So my power really did affect the gate.

00:18:10.990 --> 00:18:12.530
So you knew about that.

00:18:12.530 --> 00:18:16.070
Yeah, but I didn't want to believe it.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:19.290
Those times when you were in such pain.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:24.040
Maybe that had something
to do with the gate.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.790
I see.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:28.920
My future self wants you to...

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.760
I guess that means I was
powerless to do anything myself.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:37.050
What a loser.

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:40.470
Yuito, that's not true.

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:44.850
Kasane, there was something
I wanted to ask.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.270
If Kyoka is one of
Togetsu's Design Children,

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:51.280
does that mean you're one, too?

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:53.570
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:58.200
We saw something in Togetsu...

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:02.120
...someone with a face just like Kasane's.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:06.170
That means you <i>are </i>one, aren't you?

00:19:06.170 --> 00:19:08.880
Yes, I think you might be right.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:11.710
That's a strange choice of words.

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.970
Some memories came back to me in Togetsu.

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:18.850
Things like my childhood and my mother.

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:20.850
And in those memories,

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:23.810
I was referred to as one
of the Design Children.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:28.980
Having just remembered that,
it doesn't seem real.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:33.030
That's why my words may sound strange.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:37.660
I see. I'm sorry for bringing back
such painful memories.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:39.490
You're a kind soul, Hanabi.

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:41.910
Don't worry about it, but thank you.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:46.460
But enough about that.
Did you guys find out anything?

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.040
We heard something that sounded crazy.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:53.000
Yeah, we heard humankind
came from the moon.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:53.880
What?

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:56.050
Did you hit your head or something?

00:19:56.050 --> 00:20:00.430
Do you guys know anything
about this, Kasane?

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:02.810
Did you really hear that?

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:04.770
Um, yes.

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:07.190
We accessed some data in Togetsu.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:12.020
Humankind emigrated to the moon after
the earth's environment became unlivable.

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:13.610
And a thousand years later,

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:18.660
the group that came back to earth
supposedly founded New Himuka.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:21.410
Honestly, I find it hard to believe.

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:25.700
Kyoka, is there anything else
you can tell us about this?

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:32.630
Yes, if you're one of the Design Children
and retain Hitoyo Pope's memory...

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:35.210
I can't say for sure.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.430
I didn't retain all of
her memories, but...

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:42.140
That is historically accurate
based on what I was taught.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:45.060
Come on! Just 'cause Togetsu
says it's true--

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:48.100
Nope, that's where you're wrong.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:48.980
Huh?

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:50.980
It's all true.

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:57.190
They did emigrate to the moon, and
they did return to found New Himuka.

00:20:57.190 --> 00:20:59.780
What are you talking about, Kagero?

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:03.830
Hey now, sweet Tsugumi,
don't make that face.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.660
I'm a sucker for girls who look like that.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:10.870
Kagero, I always thought there was
something strange about you.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:12.670
Can't say I blame you.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:13.790
Huh?

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.250
Care to explain?

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:17.590
I have this vague memory.

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:21.470
I saw you ages ago, or rather, Pope did.

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:26.600
Ages ago... as in 2,000 years or so?

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:29.850
Kagero, who or what are you?

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:34.690
And what is this building?
It's not just some hideout.

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:36.400
You're a sharp one, Arashi.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:39.530
Actually, this is what we call an Ark.

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:42.360
In other words, a spaceship.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.030
A spaceship?

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:47.660
It's the one I arrived on

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:52.750
2,000 years ago as part of
the immigrant group from the moon.

00:22:07.470 --> 00:22:11.690
I will see the Sumeragi family's
dearest wish fulfilled

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:14.060
with Yuito as my tool.

00:22:22.320 --> 00:22:26.450
This time, I won't fail
to come to the rescue.

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:11.970
A 2,000-Year Ambition
